# @NAME@

Native Morph extension generated with ext SDK @SDK_VERSION@ (context ABI @ABI_VERSION@).

```sh
make
make test
make install
```

The starter builds offline with a C11 compiler and make on macOS or Linux.
It returns a fixed JSON object for empty-object input. Add a JSON library before
implementing structured arguments or dynamic output. Native calls require host
execution access in Morph.

`sdk/manifest.json` pins the SDK version, ABI and SHA-256 of every bundled header.
Commit the entire `sdk/` directory with the plugin. These are public declarations;
they contain no Morph implementation and require no Morph source or build tree.
The included nbase headers supply ABI types/status constants. If the tool starts
calling nbase functions, add an independently linked nbase dependency or validate
imports against the target host; this starter does not link a nbase implementation.

Use the development skill's `scripts/scaffold.py check .` to verify the snapshot.
SDK updates use `sdk . --sdk-version VERSION --replace` and change only `sdk/`.
SDK releases follow SemVer; existing releases remain immutable. ABI changes are
separate from Morph application versions. Check context ABI and `struct_size`,
and guard required callbacks with `EXT_HOST_HAS_CALLBACK` before calling them.
